<title>ITALY: Alenia joins Boeing, others in space group.</title>
<headline>Alenia joins Boeing, others in space group.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alenia Spazio, a unit of Italy's Finmeccanica holding company, said on Monday it had reached a deal with four major international groups to develop space station technology.</p>
<p>It said in a statement its partners were Boeing, Daimler Benz Aerospace of Germany, Japan's Mitsubishi Heavy Industries and Spar Aerospace of Canada. Alenia said it anticipated that an unnamed Russian group would join the consortium shortly.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
